      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-250151",
      ":question/problem": "Let $x$ be a Boolean variable.\n\nProve the following statement, known as the Negation Law:\n\n> $1\u2295x\u2261\u00acx$\n\nFilling in the truth tables for the left- and right-hand sides, we obtain the following:\n\n| $1$ | $x$ | $1\u2295x$ | $\u00acx$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |"
