      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-250152",
      ":question/problem": "Prove the following statement:\n\n> *Each occurrence of $\u2228$ in any principal disjunctive normal form (PDNF) can be changed to $\u2295$, keeping the new expression equivalent to the original one.*\n\nFirst, let's consider the truth tables for $\u2228$ and $\u2295$:\n\n| $x_{1}$ | $x_{2}$ | $x_{1}\u2228x_{2}$ | $x_{1}\u2295x_{2}$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | {{field-4}} |"
    }
